The C and Pascal programs below are implementations of an algorithm that puts in place a validation rule to ensure that
a valid score between 0 and 20 inclusive is input by the user.
C Program
1. #include <stdio.h>
2. int main(void) {
3. float score;
4. printf("Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20): ");
5. scanf("%f", &score);
6. while ((score < 0) || (score > 20)) {
7. printf("Enter a valid score\n");
8. printf("Enter your test score please (between 0 and 20): ");
9. scanf("%f", &score);
10. }
11. printf("Validated score entered\n");
12. getchar();
13. }
Pascal Program
